<title>SINGAPORE: Heshe shareholder sells four pct stake.</title>
<headline>Heshe shareholder sells four pct stake.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Heshe Holdings Ltd said on Thursday major shareholder Tan Seng Chai has cut his stake in the fashion retailer to 8.97 percent from 12.97 percent.</p>
<p>It said in a statement Tan had sold 11.52 million shares at Singapore $0.3315 each on July 22. Tan sold an additional 967,000 shares at S$0.34325 each on July 23, it said.</p>
<p>The company gave no reason for Tan's sale.</p>
<p>On Thursday, Heshe shares ended at S$0.35, up S$0.005 on volume of 470,000.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
